# Security (Convertly)

Checklist for auth, upload, API, secrets, and sensitive data. Limits/TTL source — [task](../../docs/technical-task.md) §7.6–7.7.

## Secrets

- Secrets from env only (`JWT_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL`, …); never hardcode.
- Do not commit `.env`, keys, or `storage/` contents.
- Do not log passwords, full API keys, file bodies, or JWTs.

## Auth & access

| Channel | Rule |
| ------- | ---- |
| SPA / account | JWT in **httpOnly** cookie (`Secure` + `SameSite` in prod); not `localStorage` |
| `/api/v1/*` | `X-API-Key`; DB stores **hash + prefix**; plaintext shown once in account UI |
| Download | signed token only (TTL **15 min**) / owner API key / share-token |
| Passwords | **argon2**; min 8 chars, letter + digit |
| Login errors | generic "Неверный email или пароль" (no which-field leak) |

Verify resource ownership (job, file, key) before sensitive operations.

## Upload & storage

- Max **10 MB**; whitelist v1 format pairs (JPG↔PNG, DOCX↔PDF).
- MIME via **magic bytes** (`file-type`), not only `Content-Type` / extension.
- No path traversal in `storage/`; never expose `storage/` as static files.
- Antivirus — out of scope v1.

## Input / ORM / XSS

- Validate DTOs (class-validator / schemas) on all inputs; whitelist, not blacklist.
- TypeORM / parameterized queries; never concatenate SQL from user input.
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization; prefer React escaping.
- Cookie session: `SameSite` (+ Nest CSRF strategy if cross-site needed).

## Rate limit (`@nestjs/throttler`)

| Channel | Limit |
| ------- | ----- |
| API convert | 30 / h / key |
| UI convert (guest) | 10 / h / IP |
| UI convert (user) | 60 / h / user |
| Login | 10 / 15 min / IP |

## Errors & deps

- Safe client messages (UI copy in Russian); stack/internals only in server logs.
- CORS — explicit SPA origin allowlist, not `*`.
- Commit `pnpm-lock.yaml`; run `pnpm audit` on dependency updates.

## Out of scope v1

Do not treat as required: 2FA, Redis rate-store, S3/CDN ACL, live Telegram Bot API, Solana/payments.
